# CrossCurrent Racing Platform — Environment Variables
#
# ⚠ Every variable below is one the CODE ACTUALLY READS. Audited 2026-08-07
# against `grep -r process.env src/ scripts/`. If you add a variable to the code,
# add it here in the same commit — a var the server doesn't know to set is
# invisible until the feature that needs it silently misbehaves.
#
# Previously this file advertised GOOGLE_SHEETS_API_KEY, GOOGLE_SHEETS_ID,
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL, DISCORD_CLIENT_ID/SECRET/CALLBACK_URL, SENTRY_DSN and
# DATADOG_API_KEY. NONE of them are read by this app — the Discord ones belong
# to `ccr-auth`, and the sheet is pulled keyless (see below). They have been
# removed rather than left as decoration: a template that lists variables which
# do nothing teaches the reader to distrust the ones that matter.

# ============================================================================
# DATABASE
# ============================================================================

# PostgreSQL connection string. Its PRESENCE is what selects the Postgres
# backend; with it unset the app falls back to a local JSON store (dev only).
# Format: postgres://user:password@host:port/database
DATABASE_URL=postgres://ccr_admin:changeme@localhost:5432/ccr_platform

# Set to "disable" to turn OFF TLS for the Postgres connection. Correct for a
# database on the same box (the production setup). Leave unset for a managed
# provider that requires TLS.
PGSSL=disable

# ============================================================================
# AUTH — the app VERIFIES, it does not log anyone in
# ============================================================================

# Where ccr-auth.service answers. Every request is verified against
# `${AUTH_SERVICE_URL}/api/auth/me` by src/middleware.ts.
#
# ⚠ THE MOST IMPORTANT VARIABLE HERE, AND IT WAS PREVIOUSLY UNDOCUMENTED.
# The middleware FAILS CLOSED: if this points somewhere unreachable, every
# request is treated as unauthenticated — browsers redirect to the Discord
# login and every API call 401s. The app looks completely broken while being
# entirely healthy. It defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8787, which is correct while
# ccr-auth runs on the same box; set it explicitly if that ever changes.
AUTH_SERVICE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787

# ============================================================================
# BENCHMARK SYNC (Ohne Speed sheet)
# ============================================================================

# The sheet is PUBLISHED-TO-WEB and pulled as keyless CSV — there is no API key
# and no Google credentials. Both values below are optional overrides for the
# hardcoded defaults; set them only if the sheet is republished under a new id
# or its master tab changes.
#   OHNE_SPEED_PUBLISHED_ID — the 2PACX-… id from the published URL
#   OHNE_SPEED_GID          — numeric tab id (default 1766901750)
OHNE_SPEED_PUBLISHED_ID=
OHNE_SPEED_GID=

# ============================================================================
# NEXT.JS
# ============================================================================

# development | production
NODE_ENV=development

# ============================================================================
# LOCAL DEV ONLY — never set these on the server
# ============================================================================

# AUTH_DEV_MODE=1 skips ccr-auth verification and authenticates every request as
# a fake local identity, so role-gated pages work on localhost (Discord OAuth can
# only complete against the real domain). DOUBLE gated: also requires a
# non-production build, so a prod build cannot compile the branch in. Put it in
# .env.local (gitignored) — NEVER in the VPS environment or the systemd unit.
AUTH_DEV_MODE=
# Role for the fake identity: driver | manager | admin (default admin)
AUTH_DEV_ROLE=

# Where the JSON dev store lives when DATABASE_URL is unset. Pins the store to
# this app's folder so a session running from another directory doesn't scatter
# a .data/ elsewhere. Irrelevant in production.
CCR_DATA_DIR=

# Base URL used by `npm run seed` (scripts/seed.mjs) when POSTing to /api/seed.
# Only needed if the app isn't on http://localhost:3000.
SEED_URL=
